$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
3-(2-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)phenyl)-1H-indole-1-carboxylate. The
product was obtained following the general procedure (0.5 mmol scale) as
white solids (191 mg, 94%) after purification by column chromatography.
mp 123-126 °C (hexanes/ EtOAc); Rf = 0.30 (5% AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 8.23 (br d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 8.13 (br d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.65
(s, 1H), 7.43-7.35 (m, 3H), 7.32 (dd, J = 7.6, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.28-7.23 (m,
1H), 7.12 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 6.54 (s, br, 1H), 1.70 (s,
9H), 1.44 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 152.9, 149.6, 136.6, 135.5, 130.8,
129.4, 128.7, 125.0, 124.5, 123.1, 122.9, 122.4, 120.2, 120.0, 117.9,
115.4, 84.1, 80.4, 28.3, 28.2; IR (KBr) νmax 3421, 3009, 2980, 2931,
1732, 1578, 1516, 1477, 1450, 1373, 1308 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z 408 (M+), 352
(M -t-Bu + H), 308 (M -Boc + 2H). Anal. Calcd for C24H28N2O4: C, 70.57;
H, 6.91; N, 6.86. Found: C, 70.78; H, 7.00; N, 6.82.
