$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2. Procedure for the Synthesis of 3-Subsituted
Pyrazinium Salts 2-Substituted pyrazines were synthesized from
2-chloropyrazine with the corresponding aryl boronic acids through
Pd-catalyzed Suzuki coupling. The substrate S1i was synthesized according
to known method. 1a The substrate S1n was synthesized using
Pd(OAc)2-BuPAd2 catalyzed Suzuki coupling. 1b The substrates S1a-d, 1c
S1f-k, 1a S1l, 1d S1m, 1e and S1n 1f were known compounds. Under nitrogen
atmosphere, 2-chloropyrazine (573 mg, 5.0 mmol), aryl boronic acid (6.5
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4(58 mg, 0.05 mmol), toluene (15.0 mL), and water (15.0
mL) were successively added to a reaction bulb. The resulted mixture was
heated to 95°C for 10 min. Then, it was cooled down to room temperature.
The potassium fluoride dihydrate (612 mg, 6.5 mmol) was added in one
portion. The reaction mixture was heated to 95 °C again. When
2-chloropyrazine was fully consumed, the mixture was cooled down and the
phases were separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate
(10 mL×2). The combined organic layer was washed with brine, dried over
sodium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo. Column chromatography of the
residue on silica gel using petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (10:1) as the
eluent. The desired coupling product S1. The yields were given in Table
1. The physical data of the new compounds were given vide infra.
2-(3,5-Dimethylphenyl)pyrazine (S1e): 866 mg, colorless oil. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.00 (s, 1H), 8.66-8.57 (m, 1H), 8.48 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H),
7.62 (s, 2H), 7.11 (s, 1H), 2.40 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
153.2, 144.1, 142.8, 142.4, 138.7, 136.3, 131.6, 124.8, 21.4. HRMS
Calculated for C12H13N2[M+H] + 185.1073, found 185.1074.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Chiral Piperazines via Hydrogenation of Pyrazines Activated
by Alkyl Halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Huang, Wen-Xue; Liu, Lian-Jin; Wu, Bo; Feng, Guang-Shou; Wang, Baomin;
Zhou, Yong-Gui
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2016), 18(13), 3082-3085

