$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Under nitrogen atmosphere, aryl boronic acid
(5.2 mmol) was added to a mixture of 2-chloro-6-methylpyrazine (514 mg,
4.0 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4(46 mg, 0.04 mmol), toluene (12.0 mL), and water
(12.0 mL). The resulted solution was heated to 95 °C for 10 min. Then, it
was cooled down to room temperature and potassium fluoride dihydrate (612
mg, 6.5 mmol) was added in one portion. The resulted mixture heated at 95
°C until 2-chloro-6-methylpyrazine was consumed. The mixture was cooled
down and the phases were separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with
ethyl acetate (10 mL×2). The combined organic layer was washed with
brine, dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo. Column
chromatography of the residue on silica gel using petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate (20:1) as the eluent. entry 8, product S3h, yield 94%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
