$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 3-Chloro-4-(3-nitrophenyl)-5-phenyl-isoxazole (6). 7d After
the mixture of 1a (153 mg, 0.5 mmol), 3-nitrophenylboronic acid (117 mg,
0.7 mmol), KHCO3 (70 mg, 0.7 mmol), and PdCl2 (5 mg, 0.025 mmol) in
DMF-H2O (4:1, 3 mL) in a Schlenk tube was degassed, it was stirred for 24
h at 80 °C under N2. Then the resultant mixture was poured into H2O (15
mL) and was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 15 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine (15 mL) and dried over Na2SO4. The solvent
was removed on a rotavapor, and the residue was purified by flash
chromatography [silica gel, 4% EtOAc in petroleum ether (60-90 °C)]. 142
mg (94%) of 6 as a white solid. Mp 118-119 °C. IR (KBr) ν 3070, 1632,
1529, 1391 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz) δ 8.32-8.27 (m, 2H), 7.72-7.64 (m, 2H),
7.52-7.50 (m, 2H), 7.48-7.45 (m, 1H), 7.41-7.37(m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz)
δ 167.6, 153.5, 148.7, 136.0, 131.2, 130.2, 129.9, 129.1 (2C), 127.0
(2C), 126.2, 124.9, 123.7, 113.0. HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): calcd for
C15H9ClN2O3, [M + H]+ 301.0374; found 301.0376. Anal. Calcd for
C15H9ClN2O3: C, 59.91; H, 3.02; N, 9.32. Found: C, 59.80; H, 3.13; N,
9.47.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tandem Synthesis of 3-Chloro-4-iodoisoxazoles from 1-Copper(I) Alkynes,
Dichloroformaldoxime, and Molecular Iodine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Wenwen; Zhang, Jianlan; Wang, Bo; Zhao, Zhouxing; Wang, Xinyan; Hu,
Yuefei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2015), 80(4), 2413-2417

